The predecessor selection is improved for most slices, but historical first-slice regeneration still emits an incorrect branch-from-tip instruction when later slices have already landed.

Review comment:

- [P2] Don't branch historical first-slice briefs from tip — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/dh2-t1b/scripts/commission-manifest.sh:427-428
  When regenerating Slice 0 after later slices have landed (`base_slice is None` and `later_landed` is non-empty), this still tells the operator this is the first slice to be cut and to branch from current `origin/main`. In that scenario `origin/main` already contains later slice merges, so the manifest includes the stale-base instruction it is trying to prevent; the origin/main instruction should only be emitted when there are no later landings, otherwise only the recovery guidance should be shown.
